-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  str_err_to_c_field.adam - Break step of str_to_c_field (PLAN-RAVENAPI F4,
  BNF sec 6; F4b): a string is stored into a C string field only where a
  hidden holder keeps its text, a field of a local or module variable (this
  module's, or another's public one) reached through value fields and
  static-array elements. Through a pointer or a deref, into a var
  parameter's record, an object's field, a dynamic array's element or a
  plain pointer variable it is SM0759 naming CString, as is a record
  literal's borrowed field where the literal goes anywhere else (an
  argument, a return, a dynamic array's element) and a dynamic array
  literal's C string element;
  returning a variable whose field holds a borrowed string, or copying it
  into a dynamic array's element or a var parameter, is SM0760. Exit 1, no
  exe.
*******************************************************************************/

/*
